{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "38345382",
      "title": "Defining Functions Inside Of Functions",
      "sourceHash": "e8648e29791ff68a1c1ea5ca211fa737a02946ac8600df2292c91dbd24d50806",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 4.89,
          "en": "Now, another thing related to functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.89,
          "end": 7.02,
          "en": "which you'll see quite a bit in this course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.02,
          "end": 11.31,
          "en": "is that you can define functions inside of functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.31,
          "end": 13.86,
          "en": "Now, when writing vanilla JavaScript code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.86,
          "end": 17.7,
          "en": "this often might not make too much sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.7,
          "end": 20.64,
          "en": "but it will make more sense in the context of React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.64,
          "end": 22.56,
          "en": "as you will see later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.56,
          "end": 25.44,
          "en": "Nonetheless, you can define a function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.44,
          "end": 27.36,
          "en": "for example, called init,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.36,
          "end": 31.14,
          "en": "which then contains another function defined inside of it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.14,
          "end": 32.91,
          "en": "for example, a function named greet",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.91,
          "end": 34.593,
          "en": "which console logs something.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.88,
          "end": 37.71,
          "en": "Then, inside of init,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.71,
          "end": 39.96,
          "en": "you can execute greet",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.96,
          "end": 43.56,
          "en": "but you can't execute greet outside of init.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.56,
          "end": 46.38,
          "en": "Because greet is now defined inside of init",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.38,
          "end": 49.26,
          "en": "and therefore it's scoped to this init function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 49.26,
          "end": 52.11,
          "en": "which means it's only available in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.11,
          "end": 56.1,
          "en": "just as a variable you would define in here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.1,
          "end": 58.35,
          "en": "would only be available inside of init",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.35,
          "end": 59.523,
          "en": "and not outside of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 60.81,
          "end": 63.51,
          "en": "And therefore, inside of init you can execute it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 63.51,
          "end": 65.91,
          "en": "but outside of init you can't.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 65.91,
          "end": 68.01,
          "en": "Here though, we can execute init",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 68.01,
          "end": 71.1,
          "en": "because init is scoped to the overall file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 71.1,
          "end": 74.583,
          "en": "since init is not nested into another function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 75.78,
          "end": 77.91,
          "en": "And therefore, with this code here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 77.91,
          "end": 79.77,
          "en": "if you reload this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 79.77,
          "end": 82.14,
          "en": "you will see that we do output hi,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 82.14,
          "end": 85.02,
          "en": "so that this code here does get executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 85.02,
          "end": 87.09,
          "en": "because in the end, we're executing this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 87.09,
          "end": 89.19,
          "en": "which then internally calls greet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 89.19,
          "end": 92.703,
          "en": "which is this function here that was defined inside of init.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 94.28999999999999,
          "end": 98.22,
          "en": "So, you are able to define and execute functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 98.22,
          "end": 100.08,
          "en": "inside of other functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 100.08,
          "end": 101.31,
          "en": "And again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 101.31,
          "end": 104.97,
          "en": "whilst this is not something you might be doing too often",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 104.97,
          "end": 107.25,
          "en": "in just JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 107.25,
          "end": 109.83,
          "en": "it is something you'll do a lot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 109.83,
          "end": 111.84,
          "en": "as you will see throughout this course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 111.84,
          "end": 113.763,
          "en": "when writing React code.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}